  "qualified_conclusions": [
    "Actual capture and ROM semantics show MAME completed one additional30fc MOVE.W before each affected IRQ stack save, whereas native completes those tile writes after the handler. SavedPC854 versus858 and savedA0 lower by2 are consistent with that operation boundary.",
    "MAME and fx68k have concretely different interrupt input/exception-latching mechanisms despite equal microcode words. These can plausibly produce software order differences without proving an RTL defect.",
    "MAME0.289 is a microcode-derived CPU with resumable bus handlers, so a blanket claim of atomic instruction-only Musashi timing is incorrect for this driver."
  ],
